{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1453083-court-contract-homebrew-help","id":1453083,"title":"Court Contract Homebrew Help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-21T14:33:49-07:00","id":1453083,"title":"Court Contract Homebrew Help","content":"So I am running a game where three of the players have founded their own courts, so I am helping them with creating court contracts. One of the three made a Court Bargain with The Death Wolf's Shadow(Rank 7 Ghost), so they were thinking about a Royal Court Contract that would raise undead warriors/summon spectral ghost warriors to fight for her. The second idea that came across was to make a variant of the Elemental Weapon contract that let them make weapons out of bones...i was curious about how to make the former work without being completely wonk and how to make the latter a bit more distinct mechanically since the whole mantle bonus is involved. Maybe making the mantle a default bonus to the base weapon or some such. Thoughts good peepz? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T13:51:50-07:00","id":1453206,"title":"","content":"I scrapped together some thoughts and came up with the following:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> a variant of the Elemental Weapon contract that let them make weapons out of bones </div> </div> </div>I designed this from the ground. I took inspiration on the name of the entity and thought about something unique that could be provided.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Fangs of the Wolf (Common)</b></span><br /> When the Lost asked for protection, The Death Wolf's Shadow showed what they could do to their enemies if they had his fangs. So they made a deal with him and now every bone used by the Changelings is a representation of the entity's fangs.<br /> <b>Cost: 2</b> Glamour<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Strenght + Survival + Mantle<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Success:</b> The Changeling can either improve his own teeth to become massive and canine like or improve two pieces of bone to become a pair of deadly daggers that remember gigantic teeth. The first option gives him a bite attack that can be used as a Brawl attack outside the grapple manuever and causes Mantle/2(rounded up) Lethal damage. The second, gives him a pair of daggers that can be used with Weaponry and cause the Bleeding Tilt (Hurt Locker page 143) with each attack, the daggers have normal statistics for daggers, but cause Mantle/2(rounded up) Lethal damage.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>The fangs or daggers causes Mantle Lethal damage, instead of Mantle/2(rounded up).<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The Contract fails.<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The fangs grow too large for the changeling body and not only cannot be used, but also inflict a penalty of -2 on his physical actions during the rest of the scene. The pair of daggers sap the vital energy from the changeling, inflicting unavoidable Mantle lethal damage on her, they can still be used after that, but the Lost feel as if his pain sated the hunger of something sinister.<br /> <b>Loophole:</b> The Lost uses bones from a recently deceased human.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> a Royal Court Contract that would raise undead warriors/summon spectral ghost warriors to fight for her. </div> </div> </div>I took inspiration from Animalism 3, that let's you summon a horde of creatures to attack something, but I changed many things to fit more into the theme of the Court. Just a friendly reminder that this would be utterly terrifying to see and possible a breaking point for witnesses.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Summon the Spectral Hunt (Royal)</b></span><br /> Even in death, the Wolf must hunt. This contract opens a brief gap on the Underworld, from wich the sons of the Wolf's Shadow slip trough. With a gesture, the Lost grabs the veil between the worlds and tore it apart, summoning spectral wolves.<br /> <b>Cost: </b>3 Glamour or 3 Glamour + 1 Willpower (see bellow)<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Occult + Mantle<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Success:</b> The veil between the worlds is ripped and spectral wolves appear in the scene, they attack one enemie pointed with zeal, trying to tore him into shreds. The wolves cause 3 bashing damage per turn and persist for the scene. They cant leave the surrounding area, so it's possible to flee from them. If a changeling spend a point of willpower, the wolves cause 2 lethal damage instead.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>The wolves are far too numerous, the changeling can designate +(Mantle) enemies to be attacked.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The barrier between the worlds is too strong. The Contract fails.<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The veil is ripped appart, but the wolves make no distinction between enemies and allies and attack the closest beings first(Usually, the user of the Contract and her allies).<br /> <b>Loophole:</b> The Lost destroys the Anchor of a ghost to open the barrier.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Please rate the contracts if possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 06-22-2021, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T09:16:16-07:00","id":1453289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1453083-court-contract-homebrew-help?p=1453206#post1453206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I scrapped together some thoughts and came up with the following:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I designed this from the ground. I took inspiration on the name of the entity and thought about something unique that could be provided.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Fangs of the Wolf (Common)</b></span><br /> When the Lost asked for protection, The Death Wolf's Shadow showed what they could do to their enemies if they had his fangs. So they made a deal with him and now every bone used by the Changelings is a representation of the entity's fangs.<br /> <b>Cost: 2</b> Glamour<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Strenght + Survival + Mantle<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Success:</b> The Changeling can either improve his own teeth to become massive and canine like or improve two pieces of bone to become a pair of deadly daggers that remember gigantic teeth. The first option gives him a bite attack that can be used as a Brawl attack outside the grapple manuever and causes Mantle/2(rounded up) Lethal damage. The second, gives him a pair of daggers that can be used with Weaponry and cause the Bleeding Tilt (Hurt Locker page 143) with each attack, the daggers have normal statistics for daggers, but cause Mantle/2(rounded up) Lethal damage.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>The fangs or daggers causes Mantle Lethal damage, instead of Mantle/2(rounded up).<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The Contract fails.<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The fangs grow too large for the changeling body and not only cannot be used, but also inflict a penalty of -2 on his physical actions during the rest of the scene. The pair of daggers sap the vital energy from the changeling, inflicting unavoidable Mantle lethal damage on her, they can still be used after that, but the Lost feel as if his pain sated the hunger of something sinister.<br /> <b>Loophole:</b> The Lost uses bones from a recently deceased human.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I took inspiration from Animalism 3, that let's you summon a horde of creatures to attack something, but I changed many things to fit more into the theme of the Court. Just a friendly reminder that this would be utterly terrifying to see and possible a breaking point for witnesses.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Summon the Spectral Hunt (Royal)</b></span><br /> Even in death, the Wolf must hunt. This contract opens a brief gap on the Underworld, from wich the sons of the Wolf's Shadow slip trough. With a gesture, the Lost grabs the veil between the worlds and tore it apart, summoning spectral wolves.<br /> <b>Cost: </b>3 Glamour or 3 Glamour + 1 Willpower (see bellow)<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Occult + Mantle<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Success:</b> The veil between the worlds is ripped and spectral wolves appear in the scene, they attack one enemie pointed with zeal, trying to tore him into shreds. The wolves cause 3 bashing damage per turn and persist for the scene. They cant leave the surrounding area, so it's possible to flee from them. If a changeling spend a point of willpower, the wolves cause 2 lethal damage instead.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>The wolves are far too numerous, the changeling can designate +(Mantle) enemies to be attacked.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The barrier between the worlds is too strong. The Contract fails.<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The veil is ripped appart, but the wolves make no distinction between enemies and allies and attack the closest beings first(Usually, the user of the Contract and her allies).<br /> <b>Loophole:</b> The Lost destroys the Anchor of a ghost to open the barrier.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Please rate the contracts if possible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks a lot man <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> i might not keep these just as you made them but they are at least excellent templates. I am a bit unsure if the Royal contract isn't a bit too expensive for what it does, but that is overall a rather minor nitpick. If you want I can send you the document where I have the courts the players made written up along with their mantle, if you want to have a gander at them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Each founder dealt with a different entity rather than doing the more conceptual patron and then tied their courts together using astrology as the system of power-sharing and the way to find commonality.<br /> <br /> The entities in question being a Fiend(Duat Denizen), A Horror from the Blue Book meant to be the embodiment of all Witches, and finally the Death Wolf's Shadow being a Ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T09:42:37-07:00","id":1453290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZPW_C4LJ6V9xQJUQcRkvDVIiZ_1wmkKj0uU6s591pGE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZPW_C4LJ6V9xQJUQcRkvDVIiZ_1wmkKj0uU6s591pGE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZPW_C4LJ6V9xQJUQcRkvDVIiZ_1wmkKj0uU6s591pGE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZPW_C4LJ6V9xQJUQcRkvDVIiZ_1wmkKj0uU6s591pGE/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Here are the courts and the motleys connected to the freehold formed around these 3 courts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T11:01:40-07:00","id":1453298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1453083-court-contract-homebrew-help?p=1453290#post1453290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZPW_C4LJ6V9xQJUQcRkvDVIiZ_1wmkKj0uU6s591pGE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Here are the courts and the motleys connected to the freehold formed around these 3 courts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for sharing, those courts look great and gave me some much needed inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T11:13:59-07:00","id":1453300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1453083-court-contract-homebrew-help?p=1453298#post1453298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for sharing, those courts look great and gave me some much needed inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> so yeah I am working on contracts that deal with their various purviews<br /> <br /> Cardinal Stars: Beginnings, Choice, Travel/Crossroads, Pain and Despair<br /> <br /> Fixed Stars: Stability, Exchanges, Family, Creation, and Nostalgia<br /> <br /> Mutable Stars: Change, Death, Secrets, Wolves, and Hate<br /> <br /> So it has been really nice getting your help here I will probably recruit errr i mean...ask for any other ideas <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}